</script>
										<script type="text/javascript">
$J( function() { InitializeCommentThread( "ForumTopic", "ForumTopic_103582791474379600_596278264013526538_592940297913236882", {"feature":"596278264013526538","feature2":"592940297913236882","owner":"103582791474379600","commentthreadid":"651527550","total_count":40,"start":15,"pagesize":15,"has_upvoted":0,"upvotes":0,"votecountid":null,"voteupid":null,"commentcountid":null,"subscribed":false,"extended_data":"{\"topic_permissions\":{\"can_view\":1,\"can_post\":1,\"can_reply\":1,\"is_banned\":0,\"can_delete\":0,\"can_edit\":0},\"original_poster\":335612007,\"topic_gidanswer\":\"0\",\"forum_appid\":2798330,\"forum_public\":1,\"forum_type\":\"General\",\"forum_gidfeature\":\"0\"}","oldestfirst":true,"comments_raw":{"592940297913307910":{"text":"[quote=BlyZeraz;592940297913279328][quote=Gandalf;592940297913254742]fuck AI but translations are one of the few things that seem acceptable to me [\/quote]\nYou'd be right that reducing language barriers would be one of the few good explorations of its usage but in its current state it's just plain incapable of that as is evident with the myriad problems that have risen from relying on machine translation for other games, shows, interviews, etc. \n\nThe fact of the matter is that even with the best intentions it can't be used yet for the task, in which case you still need to hire people with the actual level of knowledge to handle localization. I can't give a pass to them just for being indie when the end result is they made a choice that will result in a worse product for the people getting versions built off AI translations. [\/quote]\n\nIt clearly can, what you want is the perfect translation with zero errors.\nWhat people want that actually play the game is a translation good enough that you can play it and know whats going on which AI does with ease.\n\nYou say the product is a worse version, the alternative is NO product.","author":"Kamijes"},"592940297913310392":{"text":"[quote=Zero;592940297913240423]Not really generative AI, it's AI translation (with localization, though that is probably still mostly plain translation), which is pretty much what machine-translations used to be back before AI, though both are often still pretty bad (though AI translation seem to be slightly better, but that's a low bar honestly). I read a LOT of Japanese, chinese and korean works back in the day that were machine translated and they were often migraine inducing... but it was the only way to access them without spending years learning mandarin and then years learning korean and years learning Japanese on top of the other languages I already learned.\n\nSo, again, not the generative AI you might be thinking it is, which, if it were that kind of generative AI, I would also throw this game in the \"ignored\" bin for ever.\n\nEDIT: Not saying it's good, just putting it in context since the way you word it makes it seem like the game is AI, which games like that DO exist on steam btw, so valid concern [\/quote]\nNuance means nothing to ppl like the OP.","author":"Sidonus"},"592940297913310676":{"text":"[quote=UrbanNoodles;592940297913281807]We aren't your diary, Luddite. We don't really care if you have this on your ignore list. You telling us it is being ignored by you is pure attention seeking behavior.\n\nHonestly, who cares if AI was used in literally any capacity. What matters is whether the game is good or not. I could not care less that some random artist, developer, translator, or whatever other profession you want to name did not get paid for work they were never hired or asked to do in the first place. All that matters is the state of the game on release, and how the devs handle fixing any issues after release. \n\nIf AI actually makes the game worse, criticize the result. Simply saying \"AI was used\" tells me nothing about whether the game is good or not. [\/quote]\nYES.\nYa know...for gamers this used to be the one and only real standard...is it fun....now there's so many reasons to decide the game is shite 6 months out","author":"Sidonus"},"592940297913310894":{"text":"[quote=BlyZeraz;592940297913279015][quote=Horatio;592940297913247217]Luddite detected... [\/quote]\nNone of you people even know what they word means or the history of it. [\/quote]\nWtf does the history of the origin of a word that's been adopted to simply mean blanket assumptions about new things that are simply just new tools....do tools have any kind of inherent duality whatsoever...no....who wields them and how is all that matters.","author":"Sidonus"},"592940297913315267":{"text":"[quote=Sidonus;592940297913310894][quote=BlyZeraz;592940297913279015]\nNone of you people even know what they word means or the history of it. [\/quote]\nWtf does the history of the origin of a word that's been adopted to simply mean blanket assumptions about new things that are simply just new tools....do tools have any kind of inherent duality whatsoever...no....who wields them and how is all that matters. [\/quote]\n\nA hammer is going to make a terrible screwdriver no matter how much you want to pretend otherwise.\n\nLanguage evolves and people are using \"luddite\" to mean whatever they want. And they have every right to do that. Just like those of us with a modicum on education and intelligence have a right to consider the people doing it drooling morons.","author":"Only Zuul"},"592940297913316242":{"text":"[quote=Only Zuul;592940297913315267][quote=Sidonus;592940297913310894]\nWtf does the history of the origin of a word that's been adopted to simply mean blanket assumptions about new things that are simply just new tools....do tools have any kind of inherent duality whatsoever...no....who wields them and how is all that matters. [\/quote]\n\nA hammer is going to make a terrible screwdriver no matter how much you want to pretend otherwise.\n\nLanguage evolves and people are using \"luddite\" to mean whatever they want. And they have every right to do that. Just like those of us with a modicum on education and intelligence have a right to consider the people doing it drooling morons. [\/quote]\nuh....right lol","author":"Sidonus"},"592940297913321139":{"text":"[quote=BlyZeraz]I remember keeping tabs on this one now and then over the past few months but seeing the AI disclosure added now just erased any interest. Welcome to the ignore list. Not just the game but your dev and publisher pages too. [\/quote]\nSo basically, you checked your pockets, noticed your broke, and now you need to find an excuse for yourself why you did Not want to buy it anyway? Rrrrriiiiiiight?","author":"Rammstein"},"592940297913323447":{"text":"people throwing around the world \"luddite\" as if it's a defense for modern \"ai\" being shit in almost every aspect...","author":"LuviTheAvali"},"592940297913327194":{"text":"Nice ragebite","author":"Hains"},"592940297913331522":{"text":"OP IS CAVEMAN. UG!   \u02d0buzzed\u02d0","author":"labtob"},"592940297913331604":{"text":"so what are the languages that use AI translation anyways?","author":"Secrom36"},"592940297913342171":{"text":"If you're anti LLM at this point I think its best you just delete steam.  Any modern software team is using AI for all sorts of things.  It's much much better at writing code than most humans.  What so you think valve programmers are doing right now?  Typing code by hand \ud83e\udd23?!","author":"internetgrout"},"592940297913343674":{"text":"The only thing you're doing is discouraging disclosure. I applaud the devs for clearly labelling their work.\nI'm anti-AI too, but this usage of it is harmless. It's better for us to know what parts were made by humans, rather than just wonder, right?","author":"Rodrik Forrester"},"592940297913351574":{"text":"Op basically negative reviews 95% of the sh*t he plays.\n\nSo I don't know why lil' bro is even playing video games at this point lmao.\n\nBrother is f*ckin' miserable it seems.","author":"Wolfy"},"592940297913351777":{"text":"[quote=Wolfy;592940297913351574]Op basically negative reviews 95% of the sh*t he plays.\n\nSo I don't know why lil' bro is even playing video games at this point lmao.\n\nBrother is f*ckin' miserable it seems. [\/quote]\nTheyre everywhere, and they all are miserable","author":"Sidonus"}},"track_navigation":true}, 'https://steamcommunity.com/comment/ForumTopic/', 40 ); } );
</script>
