			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_592940297913307910">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c592940297913279328">BlyZeraz</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c592940297913254742">Gandalf</a></b>:</div>♥♥♥♥ AI but translations are one of the few things that seem acceptable to me </blockquote>You'd be right that reducing language barriers would be one of the few good explorations of its usage but in its current state it's just plain incapable of that as is evident with the myriad problems that have risen from relying on machine translation for other games, shows, interviews, etc. <br><br>The fact of the matter is that even with the best intentions it can't be used yet for the task, in which case you still need to hire people with the actual level of knowledge to handle localization. I can't give a pass to them just for being indie when the end result is they made a choice that will result in a worse product for the people getting versions built off AI translations. </blockquote><br>It clearly can, what you want is the perfect translation with zero errors.<br>What people want that actually play the game is a translation good enough that you can play it and know whats going on which AI does with ease.<br><br>You say the product is a worse version, the alternative is NO product.			</div>
