			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_592940297913310392">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c592940297913240423">Zero</a></b>:</div>Not really generative AI, it's AI translation (with localization, though that is probably still mostly plain translation), which is pretty much what machine-translations used to be back before AI, though both are often still pretty bad (though AI translation seem to be slightly better, but that's a low bar honestly). I read a LOT of Japanese, chinese and korean works back in the day that were machine translated and they were often migraine inducing... but it was the only way to access them without spending years learning mandarin and then years learning korean and years learning Japanese on top of the other languages I already learned.<br><br>So, again, not the generative AI you might be thinking it is, which, if it were that kind of generative AI, I would also throw this game in the &quot;ignored&quot; bin for ever.<br><br>EDIT: Not saying it's good, just putting it in context since the way you word it makes it seem like the game is AI, which games like that DO exist on steam btw, so valid concern </blockquote>Nuance means nothing to ppl like the OP.			</div>
