				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c592940297913310894">Sidonus</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c592940297913279015">BlyZeraz</a></b>:</div>None of you people even know what they word means or the history of it. </blockquote>Wtf does the history of the origin of a word that's been adopted to simply mean blanket assumptions about new things that are simply just new tools....do tools have any kind of inherent duality whatsoever...no....who wields them and how is all that matters. </blockquote><br>A hammer is going to make a terrible screwdriver no matter how much you want to pretend otherwise.<br><br>Language evolves and people are using &quot;luddite&quot; to mean whatever they want. And they have every right to do that. Just like those of us with a modicum on education and intelligence have a right to consider the people doing it drooling morons.			</div>
